{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts","id":771153,"title":"Sidereals, the Mastery keyword, Sutras, and Sidereal Martial Arts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-21T19:40:16-08:00","id":771153,"title":"Sidereals, the Mastery keyword, Sutras, and Sidereal Martial Arts","content":"Various related ideas, here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mastery: </b>This keyword denotes [Martial Arts] Charms that have a greater effect when used by those Exalted who are masters of mortal Abilities: the Solar and Abyssal Exalted. <b>The Sidereal Exalted, peerless masters of the martial arts, have their own esoteric methods for accessing these effects. (emphasis mine)</b> </div> </div> </div><b>My Predictions:</b><br /> <br /> * Sidereals will use Sutras to access the Solar levels of Mastery-keyworded Martial Arts Charms, which is much less hilariously broken or impossible to balance than the huge mote-cost discounts provided in the two previous Editions.<br /> <br /> * Sidereals will now be able to employ Sutras with <i>every single Martial Art Style</i> in the game, not just Violet Bier of Sorrows or Sidereal-level Styles. (Which incidentally means that Violet Bier of Sorrows loses the very last mechanical reason to be native Sidereal Charms, since it can keep its Sutra.)<br /> <br /> * Each Style only gets ONE Sutra for the Style as a whole, rather than a Student and a Master pair, since each Style has a varying number of Mastery-keyworded Charms before and after the Form Charm, and not every Form Charm itself has the keyword, which means that the old Student Sutras will sometimes be nearly useless with one Style compared to another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>My question:</b><br /> <br /> Now that the game line is avoiding Charms over Essence 5+, and now that Sidereals can elevate any &quot;Terrestrial-level Style&quot; or &quot;Celestial-level Style&quot; to the level of the Blossom of the Perfected Lotus (Solar/Sidereal), is there any room for the Sidereal Martial Arts Styles as we've known them?<br /> <br /> They could be brought down to a level just above normal Styles, lacking any Terrestrial keyword (or applying that keyword to Lunars!*), and with the Sutra keyword locking Solars as well as Sidereals out of the full benefits of certain Charms unless the Stylist uses a Sutra. Which might only be available to Sidereals, as before.<br /> <br /> They could even become completely normal Styles and still function largely as before -- Anys Sin cannot enlighten Dragon-Blooded sufficiently to access the Mastery/Sutra-gated effects of any Charm without them exploding, just as she couldn't do with Righteous Devil or White Reaper Style. (Would Dragon-Blooded even get to enjoy Mastery level control of the Immaculate Dragon Styles, or would Sidereals perform it better with Sutras while Terrestrials must content themselves with avoiding the limitation of the Terrestrial keyword?)<br /> <br /> <br /> * This is a throw-away thought; I still don't care if Lunars ever get Sidereal Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-21-2015, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T20:28:55-08:00","id":771181,"title":"","content":"Doesn't that imply writing sutras for every single MA style that gets published between now and the Sidereal book coming out? Seems really labour intensive (even by 3e standards!) for no real benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T20:58:44-08:00","id":771200,"title":"","content":"Sutras being used to attain Mastery sounds plausible to me. They don't actually have to write the sutras, they just have to say that they exist.<br /> <br /> But I'm pretty sure SMA isn't going anywhere. It's too cool and too iconic to discard. Plus, it's referenced in the Corebook.<br /> <br /> Selfsame Master Instruction says you can't teach SMA, and Sidereal Martial Arts are mentioned in the Sidereal blurb at the start of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":1154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","user":"Sanctaphrax","date":". 11-22-2015, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T21:27:58-08:00","id":771209,"title":"","content":"I noticed that nearly all Martial Arts trees only go up as far as Essence 3.<br /> <br /> So SMA as Essence 4 and 5 Martial Arts charms seems to be fine, in terms of them having a place.<br /> <br /> It also means you'll have to likely combine SMA and normal MA; SMA to get the crazy esoteric effects, regular MA to get the normal bread-and-butter stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:32:52-08:00","id":771240,"title":"","content":"I would rather something like:<br /> Sidereals are able to buy Martial Arts without the merit (equivalently, they get the merit for free) but don't gain the Mastery benefit<br /> Upon buying the Martial Arts merit (or equivalently, some new 4-dot merit called &quot;Mastery&quot;) Sidereals gain the Mastery benefit<br /> <br /> I don't think Solars should be <i>better</i> than Sidereals at Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:50:28-08:00","id":771247,"title":"","content":"While I have no objection to them having Mastery, I also wouldn't object to them instead having access to weird SMA that are better (in the way high Essence charms are better than low Essence charms). So they're not quite as good as a Solar at just punching you in the face, but hey, a Solar can't punch you in your intimacies.<br /> So not really worse or be\u200btter, just different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T23:09:46-08:00","id":771253,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, now that Martial Arts is an ability outside the standard list of 25, I think every Sidereal should get it favoured.<br /> <br /> It's such a big part of the splat that I expect almost everyone to want it, and Endings Sidereals get Caste Brawl now so everyone will have 5 Caste abilities anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T23:45:39-08:00","id":771272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771200#post771200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't actually have to write the sutras, they just have to say that they exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771240#post771240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Solars should be <i>better</i> than Sidereals at Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too bad, because Martial Arts is an Ability. Why do you think Sidereals need to DO something to attain Mastery effects when the Solars just automatically get them?<br /> <br /> Sidereals can do <i>some </i>things regarding Martial Arts better than Solars, but they can't do Martial Arts better <i>in general</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771253#post771253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, now that Martial Arts is an ability outside the standard list of 25, I think every Sidereal should get it favoured.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a terrible solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Endings Sidereals get Caste Brawl now </div> </div> </div>Based on what? I'm pretty sure I have an entire different thread dedicated to arguing that Endings should get Presence, since Sidereal Presence lost all of its Charms to Sidereal War, and it would better to write up a bunch of new Endings-flavored Presence Charms than to toss out all of the Battles-flavored Brawl Charms.<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet is the perfect constellation for Brawl, not Presence. The Banner originally assigned to Presence is perfect for War, and Presence would fit very well under the threatening Sword -- persuading someone at swordpoint, or the enlightening argument of the Sword of Damocles.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Endings Caste aren't about combat; the Battles Caste are about combat. The Martial Arts are literally named after the deity of War.<br /> <br /> Insofar as the Endings Caste are about causing death, poisoning someone with Medicine, legally signing their death warrant with Bureaucracy, and convincing someone to murder them with Presence are all just as perfectly valid methods. Death as a result of combat is Mars/Battles.<br /> <br /> The Sword constellation was never about the &quot;emulation&quot; side of Martial Arts; it was about Violet Bier of Sorrows, which no longer works as a native Charm tree, if it ever did; Snake Style and Five Dragon Style were never native, and they're certainly not now.<br /> <br /> The Sword constellation can't be MADE about the Martial Arts in general, either, because when you make the Executioner's Sword into the Duelist's Sword, it becomes Mars' Sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-22-2015, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:02:29-08:00","id":771278,"title":"","content":"My pet theory for Sidereal Martial Arts is that it doesn't use Martial Arts at all. Charcoal MArch of Spiders is an Athletics Martial Art. It uses Athletics instead of Martial Arts. Citrine Poxes of Contagion is a Medicine Martial Art. You attack and defend and etc. using Medicine instead of Martial Arts. Etc etc etc. Martial Arts Supernal covers all Sidereal Martial Arts while supernal in an ability lets you get sidereal martial arts keyed to that ability.<br /> <br /> I do not actually think I am correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:03:51-08:00","id":771280,"title":"","content":"Man, I <i>hope</i> I don't have to have 2-300 XP to <i>start</i> delving into the secrets of Sidereal Martial Arts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:04:18-08:00","id":771281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771247#post771247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I have no objection to them having Mastery, I also wouldn't object to them instead having access to weird SMA that are better (in the way high Essence charms are better than low Essence charms). So they're not quite as good as a Solar at just punching you in the face, but hey, a Solar can't punch you in your intimacies.<br /> So not really worse or be\u200btter, just different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the way Celestial Monkey changes is even more drastic than expected, then there will likely still at least one Style for Solars to punch people in the intimacies due to the fact that Virtues no longer exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:18:08-08:00","id":771289,"title":"","content":"I *do* think Sidereals needs to be able to start with Sidereal Martial Arts. Everyone always wanted to start with it when playing Sidereals, to the point that not having it felt *really* weird. I say this having played a Sidereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T02:14:58-08:00","id":771335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there any room for the Sidereal Martial Arts Styles as we've known them?</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on how much of what we've known of them one is attached to. Personally, I'm looking for Sidereal Martial Arts which take a lot of the iconic effects of the prior Editions, break them down, blend them together, and wind up with something where Charcoal March of Spiders has punching a lot of people at once and/or transforming their Essence with a punch by the culmination of a chain of setup actions (my own picture is of wrapping them up in your webs, but I can go with whatever). Similar with inflicting freaky diseases or breaking minds. I think Obsidian Shards can more readily distribute weird reflection powers across its entire tree without needing to basically be its own system now, and I was never really able to wrap my head around Prismatic Arrangement to know what it did, so I can't really say how it would transcribe. My point is, I think it's simple enough to scale the Sidereal Arts down enough while still being distinctly psychedelic, and I certainly think there's room to actually make them function as Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:58:23-08:00","id":771371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771200#post771200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't actually have to write the sutras, they just have to say that they exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty unconvinced, to me the whole point of sutras is that we know what they say and that there's a deeper meaning that may be reflected by the attitudes and outlooks of the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> It seems weird to adopt the pre-existing approach to scriptures and prayer strips and then essentially answer the question of &quot;so what does my Crane Stylist write on her prayer strips when she knows she faces a difficult battle?&quot; with &quot;we don't know ...it doesn't matter&quot; when it'd apparently matter if you were using Melee or Archery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:21:08-08:00","id":771494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771272#post771272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what? I'm pretty sure I have an entire different thread dedicated to arguing that Endings should get Presence, since Sidereal Presence lost all of its Charms to Sidereal War, and it would better to write up a bunch of new Endings-flavored Presence Charms than to toss out all of the Battles-flavored Brawl Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the assumption that they're sticking with the current Ability setup. Might be wrong. But even if it is wrong, the basic point is the same: everyone gets 5 Caste abilities once you give favoured MA out for free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771289#post771289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I *do* think Sidereals needs to be able to start with Sidereal Martial Arts. Everyone always wanted to start with it when playing Sidereals, to the point that not having it felt *really* weird. I say this having played a Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, FWIW. Obviously this is a matter of taste, but I like having SMA at higher Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771371#post771371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty unconvinced, to me the whole point of sutras is that we know what they say and that there's a deeper meaning that may be reflected by the attitudes and outlooks of the Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly part of the point. But sutras are also vehicles for mechanical bonuses. And they can serve that role even if their text is mysterious.<br /> <br /> Actually, I just had an idea. Maybe normal Martial Arts don't have a pre-defined deeper meaning. But Sidereals can make up deeper meanings, writing their own sutras to access the greater secrets of the style.<br /> <br /> So for Crane Style, one Sidereal might use a sutra about peace and another might use a sutra about a wise teacher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:33:45-08:00","id":771503,"title":"","content":"This seems like one of those things where its sort of a shame the Techniques system went, because then we could've had Sidereals hanging Sidereal Charms off Techniques, and Solars, DBs the same (while Lunars wouldn't really hang Charms off Techniques so much as use them with synergy with Attribute Charms).<br /> <br /> Rather than needing to fit this kind of keywords system that suggests tier hierarchies while the new edition is supposed to be embracing the potential in Exalted who are built on using different essence more than being +1, +2 to one another (and it just happens Solar Essence is naturally strongest).<br /> <br /> Understand why it went though! I still don't aesthetically like how Exalted does MA though.<br /> <br /> I don't think Sidereals using Sutras to access Solar Mastery effects seems like a very good idea. They can just buy some Sidereal only SMA and combine it or something. I still quite like the idea of SMA covering some effects which are similar in scope and form and perhaps conditions to invoke and acquire to Evocations (and a good use for the &quot;Sidereal XP&quot; they also can also use on Astrology and Sorcery, if that is a mechanic for them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T03:38:31-08:00","id":772200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771272#post771272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad, because Martial Arts is an Ability. Why do you think Sidereals need to DO something to attain Mastery effects when the Solars just automatically get them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing the Sidereal needs to do may range from &quot;Spend an action powering up in combat&quot; to &quot;say that they did some fancy thing in training that never gets referenced again&quot;. We have no details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 11-23-2015, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T07:32:54-08:00","id":772282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/771153-sidereals-the-mastery-keyword-sutras-and-sidereal-martial-arts?p=771272#post771272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad, because Martial Arts is an Ability. Why do you think Sidereals need to DO something to attain Mastery effects when the Solars just automatically get them?<br /> <br /> Sidereals can do <i>some </i>things regarding Martial Arts better than Solars, but they can't do Martial Arts better <i>in general</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing sidereals shoudn't be doing better than solars, when it comes to martial arts, is geting an advantage in terms of number of statistical success rolled.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, sidereals should be able to do anything at least as good and as efficiently as a solar (no mote surcharge etc...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}